WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.506
Photos, videos, maps, navigation artifacts, significant locations at a high level, Wi-Fi context, Bluetooth context, and health or fitness app data can all provide investigative leads.

2
00:00:12.506 --> 00:00:17.933
These artifacts may help place a device, account, or application into a timeline.

3
00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:28.316
They should also be treated with caution because location and sensor records can be incomplete, approximate, synced, or generated by background behavior.

4
00:00:28.316 --> 00:00:36.496
Media files may contain EXIF metadata depending on how the file was created, edited, transmitted, saved, or synchronized.

5
00:00:36.496 --> 00:00:43.103
EXIF can include camera information, timestamps, device-related fields, and sometimes geotags.

6
00:00:43.103 --> 00:00:50.811
But metadata can be stripped, altered, absent, copied from another source, or affected by application processing.

7
00:00:50.811 --> 00:00:55.609
It should support a conclusion only when the surrounding evidence fits.

8
00:00:55.609 --> 00:01:04.104
Maps and navigation artifacts may include searches, destinations, recent places, routes, cached data, or application state.

9
00:01:04.104 --> 00:01:15.194
Significant locations, where available and authorized, should be treated at a high level as a source of possible location context, not as a complete movement history.

10
00:01:15.194 --> 00:01:21.565
Settings, retention, precision, app behavior, and account sync can all change what is present.

11
00:01:21.565 --> 00:01:26.442
Wi-Fi and Bluetooth context can help explain environment and proximity.

12
00:01:26.442 --> 00:01:38.633
Known networks, connection records, paired devices, or nearby device references may support a timeline, but they do not always prove a person was present or intentionally connected.

13
00:01:38.633 --> 00:01:48.386
Health and fitness data may also provide timing, movement, or activity context, but it can depend on sensors, watches, apps, and synchronization.

14
00:01:48.386 --> 00:01:52.083
Time zones and timestamp normalization are essential.

15
00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:59.791
iOS artifacts may use different time formats, precision levels, local time, UTC, or application-specific values.

16
00:01:59.791 --> 00:02:10.252
Location evidence should be corroborated with media, account logs, application records, network data, witness statements, or other independent sources.

17
00:02:10.252 --> 00:02:16.702
Reports should describe precision and uncertainty rather than overstating location findings.
